>> title: English Muffins
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, breakfast, griddle, milk, yeast
>> counters: Diner, Bakery
>> pairs-with: hollandaise
>> servings: 8
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: narrow — the griddle stays low for seven minutes a side; one that browns before the middle sets is raw in the centre and burnt outside

>> step: stir, stand 10 min
Stir @warm whole milk{1 1/4%cup}(300 mL) with @granulated sugar{1%Tbs}(12 g) and @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), then let stand ~{10%min}.

>> step: beat to a soft dough
Beat @bread flour{3 1/4%cup}(440 g), @table salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g), and @softened unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g) into @&(~1)yeast mixture{}.

>> step: cover, rise until doubled
Cover @&(~1)dough{} and rise until doubled, ~{1 1/2%hours}.

>> step: roll 1/2 in, cut eight rounds, proof 45 min
Roll @&(~1)dough{} 1/2 in thick, cut eight rounds, dust with @cornmeal{3%Tbs}, then proof ~{45%min}.

>> step: griddle over low heat 7 min a side
Cook @&(~1)muffins{} on a #griddle{} filmed with @vegetable oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) for ~{7%min} a side.
